EXT. TOLL BRIDGE OVER A MISTY GORGE - DAWN

Ropes and rotted planks span a chasm. Mist swallows the far end. A lantern hangs from a crooked post.

WYNDRA, a sorceress in grey robes, stands at the center of the bridge. Beside her, SIR OSRIC, an old knight in dented armor, leans on his sword. THISBE, a young thief with a quick grin, crouches at the rail, picking the lock of a small chest. GRIMBOLD, a squat troll in a toll collector's cap, blocks the path ahead. MARROW, a wolf the size of a pony, circles behind him.

GRIMBOLD
Three coins each.

She reaches into her robe. He draws his sword a hand's breadth. She smiles and produces a single silver coin, which she tosses in a high arc over the gorge. The troll watches it fall. Marrow lunges.

Thisbe vaults the rail and kicks the wolf in the ribs. He yelps. The troll swings his club and the old knight blocks it with his shield. The planks groan.

OSRIC
Enough! We have no quarrel!

WYNDRA
Put down your weapons.

She lifts one hand. The mist thickens. The club slows in midair. Marrow whimpers and sits. The troll lowers his cap over his eyes.

GRIMBOLD
(grumbling)
Two coins, then.
